#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# vector_angle

#% text
# `vector_angle(u, v)` gives the angle between the vectors `u` and `v`, `acos(u . conjugate(v)/(|u| |v|))`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The angle lies between 0 and `pi`.

#% item
# Exact vectors give exact angles when the cosine is a known value.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
vector_angle([1, 0], [1, 1])
#% output
#= (1/4)*pi

#% cell
vector_angle([1, 0, 0], [0, 1, 0])
#% output
#= (1/2)*pi

#% cell
vector_angle([1, 2, 3], [-1, 0, 2])
#% output
#= acos((1/14)*70^(1/2))

#% cell
vector_angle([1., 2.], [2., 1.])
#% output
#= 0.6435011087932844

#% cell
vector_angle([a, b], [x, y])
#% output
#= acos((a*conjugate(x) + b*conjugate(y))/((abs(a)^2 + abs(b)^2)^(1/2)*(abs(x)^2 + abs(y)^2)^(1/2)))

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `angle_vector`, `dot`, `norm`
